(i)
"Critical shipboard operation" means operations which are likely to cause an accident or a situation threatening the
safety of the people, the environment or the ship;
(j)
"Designated person" means a person ashore with direct access to the highest level of management, charged with the
responsibility and the authority to monitor the safety and pollution aspects of the operation of each ship;
(k)
"Document of compliance" means a Certificate of Compliance issued by the Director General of Shipping to a Company;
(l)
"Gas carrier" means a cargo ship constructed or adapted and used for the carriage in bulk of any liquefied gas or other
product listed in the International Gas Carrier Code;
(m)
"High speed craft" means a craft capable of maximum speed in metres per seconds equal to or exceeding 3.7 ? 0.1667 ,
